-- title:
--   Norms of conjugate products at an unramified place
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers $\mathcal O_K$, and let $w$ be an extension of $v$ to $\mathcal O_L$, that is, a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_L$ whose contraction to $\mathcal O_K$ is $v$. Assume that the ramification index of $w$ over its contraction to $\mathcal O_K$ equals $1$. Let $n$ denote $\dim_{K_v} L_w$, the rank of the completion $L_w$ at $w$ as a module over the completion $K_v$ at $v$, and let $\theta$ be an automorphism of $L_w$ as a $K_v$-algebra. Let $\alpha \in L_w^{\times}$ and $a \in K_v^{\times}$ be units satisfying $\prod_{i=0}^{n-1} \theta^{i}(\alpha) = a$, the right-hand side being the image of $a$ under the structure map $K_v \to L_w$. The conclusion is that there exists an integer $r$ with $\lVert \alpha \rVert = (\mathrm{absNorm}\, w)^{-r}$ and $\lVert a \rVert = (\mathrm{absNorm}\, v)^{-n r}$, the norms being those of the canonical valuations on $L_w$ and $K_v$ and $\mathrm{absNorm}$ the absolute ideal norm.
--
--   This is the local norm bookkeeping at an unramified place: the normalised absolute value of a unit lies in the value group generated by the residue norm, automorphisms over $K_v$ are isometries, and the $w$-norm restricts to the $n$-th power of the $v$-norm when $e(w/v)=1$. It is used in the inert-place reduction, by [`AutomorphicForm.twistedWeighted_eq_finrank_mul_weighted_heckeWord_of_inertiaDeg_eq_finrank`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.twistedWeighted_eq_finrank_mul_weighted_heckeWord_of_inertiaDeg_eq_finrank), to match valuation exponents of a local unit and of its norm.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_norm_eq_zpow_and_norm_eq_zpow_of_prod_algEquiv_pow_eq.lean

